 "about": "ADR-0061: the signed bytes of a device endorsement (agora-device-endorse-v1) and revocation (agora-device-revoke-v1), and the fingerprint people compare. Checked by the node (crates/agora-node/src/device_trust.rs), the terminal client (crates/agora-tui/src/device.rs) and the web window (apps/web/src/net/devices.test.ts). Every field is `<decimal byte length>:<UTF-8 bytes>`; the public key is written as lowercase hex; `nodes` is its count, then each node. `signature` is a valid ES256 signature (r || s) of `hex` by `endorser_public_key` (test key, never trusted anywhere). Registrations (agora-device-register-v1: device id, name, key in hex, signed_at_ms) and asks (agora-device-ask-v1: device id, signed_at_ms) are signed by the device own key (here the same test key). A fingerprint is the first 12 bytes (96 bits) of the SHA-256 of the 65-byte key, lowercase hex in groups of 4 hex digits joined by `-`.",
